---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CollectionIcon from '../components/CollectionIcon.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import polaroid from '../assets/suprlab-polaroid.png';
import posts from '../data/posts.json';
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const projects=posts.filter(p=>p.type==='post'&&p.tags.some(t=>t.slug==='project-journal'));
---
<Layout><section class="hero wrap"><div class="hero-copy"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="cross">✳</span> <span>BITS, BOARDS & BLEEPS</span></div><h1>A place for things<br/>worth <em>making.</em></h1><div class="hero-bottom"><p><span class="accent-blue">Small devices.</span> <span class="accent-orange">Long nights.</span><br/>Independent projects, useful guides, and build notes.</p><a class="text-link" href="#projects">Explore the projects <span class="plus">+</span></a></div></div><figure class="hero-polaroid"><Image src={polaroid} widths={[280, 560, 840]} sizes="(max-width: 800px) 240px, (max-width: 1100px) 230px, 280px" width={280} alt="Illustrated portrait of dean with colourful retro gaming and music doodles, framed as a Polaroid captioned BUILD. TINKER. REPEAT." format="webp" quality={85} loading="eager" /></figure></section>
<section id="projects" class="wrap section"><div class="section-heading"><h2>On the <span class="accent-orange">workbench</span></h2><span class="mono">SELECTED PROJECTS</span></div><div class="featured-grid"><article class="project-card slot"><a class="project-visual slot-visual" href={`${base}projects/slot-advance/`}><img src={`${base}projects/slot-advance.webp`} alt="slot.advance firmware on an open Anbernic RG SP handheld" fetchpriority="high"/><span class="image-label">GBA, WITH INTENTION.</span></a><div class="project-content"><div class="project-meta"><span>FIRMWARE / RETRO GAMING</span><span>ANBERNIC RG SP</span></div><h3><a href={`${base}projects/slot-advance/`}>slot.advance</a></h3><p>A little more Game Boy. A little less friction. GBA-focused firmware with real hardware sleep, instant resume and saves that travel with you.</p><div class="project-links"><a href={`${base}projects/slot-advance/`}>Explore project</a><a href="https://github.com/slowphase/slot.advance">Repository</a></div></div></article><article class="project-card fm1"><a class="project-visual fm1-visual" href={`${base}projects/fm1-pocket-player/`}><img src={`${base}projects/fm1-hero.jpg`} alt="FM-1 Pocket Player — play, explore, discover"/><span class="image-label">A SMALL BOX. A LOT OF SOUND.</span></a><div class="project-content"><div class="project-meta"><span>WEB AUDIO / MUSIC</span><span>IN YOUR BROWSER</span></div><h3><a href={`${base}projects/fm1-pocket-player/`}>FM-1 Pocket Player</a></h3><p>A playground for the M-VAVE FM-1. Explore community firmware, turn the knobs, and make some noise. No hardware required.</p><div class="project-links"><a href="https://slowphase.github.io/fm1-pocket-player/">Play in your browser</a><a href={`${base}projects/fm1-pocket-player/`}>Explore project</a></div></div></article></div></section>
<section class="wrap section collections"><div class="section-heading"><h2>A little further down the <span class="accent-yellow">rabbit hole</span></h2><span class="mono">COLLECTIONS</span></div><div class="collection-grid"><a class="collection guides" href={`${base}guides/`}><div class="collection-top"><CollectionIcon /><span class="mono">FIELD NOTES</span></div><h3>The GitHub guides</h3><p>Practical documentation, setup notes and things learned the long way. Collected in one place.</p><span class="collection-bottom">Browse the guides <span>+</span></span></a><a class="collection archive" href={`${base}projects/`}><div class="collection-top"><CollectionIcon /><span class="mono">BUILD LOGS</span></div><h3>The project journals</h3><p>An ambient AWTRIX display and an Endgame Switch Lite. Two hardware builds, with all their notes.</p><span class="collection-bottom">Explore {projects.length} projects <span>+</span></span></a></div></section>
<section class="wrap outro"><span class="cross">✳</span><p>Curiosity is the whole point.</p><span class="mono">AN INDEPENDENT WORK IN PROGRESS.</span></section></Layout>
